WEBVTT

00:07.230 --> 00:12.260
<b>This is a work of fiction. The names of the people, places, and organizations
are fictitious and in no way related to any real person or entity.</b>

00:14.460 --> 00:16.700
Well, well... It's spring, all right.

00:19.130 --> 00:22.680
It's already our second spring 
since becoming third-years.

00:23.610 --> 00:24.270
Hm?

00:24.580 --> 00:26.710
More importantly, Onee-chan...

00:26.710 --> 00:27.500
What?

00:27.870 --> 00:32.260
Tomorrow's the sports festival. 
Should you really be relaxing here?

00:34.590 --> 00:40.160
I'm not like those other student council 
presidents! I'm actually super efficient!

00:40.160 --> 00:42.400
I already laid out a solid plan in advance

00:42.400 --> 00:46.060
and finished getting ready 
for everything yesterday!

00:46.060 --> 00:47.520
You're the best, Onee-chan!

00:47.740 --> 00:50.070
I'm sure all those other 
student council presidents

00:50.070 --> 00:53.900
are panicking and flailing around right 
about now, like grade-school kids

00:53.900 --> 00:57.280
who put off their summer homework 
until the very end of summer vacation!

00:58.320 --> 01:00.030
We've got trouble, President!

02:30.000 --> 02:35.000
<b>Get the Sports Festival Done!</b>

02:30.000 --> 02:35.000
<b>Get the Sports Festival Done!</b>

02:35.220 --> 02:36.760
We've got trouble, President!

02:37.310 --> 02:38.950
What's the matter, Nekoyamada-san?

02:38.950 --> 02:42.760
Some of the relay batons broke, 
and now we don't have enough!

02:42.760 --> 02:45.150
I see. Fear not.

02:45.150 --> 02:49.320
I figured something like this might happen, 
so I bought extras. We can use those.

02:49.320 --> 02:50.950
You're the best, Onee-chan!

02:52.100 --> 02:53.770
There are no holes in my plan.

02:53.770 --> 02:58.360
P-P-President! Some of the number bibs 
got ripped, and now we don't have enough!

02:58.360 --> 02:59.060
Huh?

02:59.060 --> 03:02.610
I-I-I'm probably being punished for 
only pretending to eat my bell peppers

03:02.610 --> 03:05.870
and putting them on my dad's plate last night!

03:06.090 --> 03:08.880
Calm down. That has nothing to do with this.

03:08.880 --> 03:11.370
It's all right. I have extras of those, 
too, so we can just...

03:11.670 --> 03:14.500
President! The giant ball for the 
giant ball roll has disappeared!

03:14.740 --> 03:15.500
Huh?

03:15.500 --> 03:18.840
President! The computer where the 
sports festival schedule was saved

03:18.840 --> 03:20.630
just broke for no reason!

03:20.630 --> 03:21.630
Wha?

03:21.630 --> 03:24.890
President! Oshio-kun from the 
executive committee disappeared!

03:24.890 --> 03:28.390
President! A kitten climbed up 
a tree and can't get back down!

03:28.390 --> 03:32.140
President! A fawn climbed up 
another tree and can't get back down!

03:32.140 --> 03:34.720
Wait, wait, wait, just a...

03:32.140 --> 03:35.650
<b>Deer Crackers</b>

03:33.360 --> 03:34.720
President.

03:36.090 --> 03:38.650
The admission gate fell over 
and was destroyed.

03:38.890 --> 03:42.120
Huh? What?!

03:41.950 --> 03:43.160
<b>Admission Gate</b>

03:44.900 --> 03:46.180
Wh-Wh-Where do I even start?!

03:46.180 --> 03:47.810
The admission gate first, right?

03:47.810 --> 03:50.060
Or the giant ball? Wait, maybe Oshio?

03:50.060 --> 03:52.470
No, the kitten... Or maybe the fawn?

03:52.470 --> 03:54.250
What?!

03:54.520 --> 03:57.390
Koshitan, you're like a grade-school kid

03:57.390 --> 04:00.520
who put off her summer homework 
until the very end of summer vacation.

04:03.690 --> 04:06.010
Fine! I need you all to help me!

04:06.280 --> 04:07.310
Aw...

04:07.310 --> 04:09.910
Don't "Aw..." me! You absolutely have time!

04:09.910 --> 04:12.380
Bashame does not have time.

04:12.380 --> 04:12.770
Huh?

04:13.330 --> 04:16.110
Bashame needs to prepare 
for tomorrow's rice planting.

04:16.360 --> 04:18.500
Why are you planting rice 
during a school festival?!

04:18.500 --> 04:20.730
Save it for when you have nothing better to do!

04:21.170 --> 04:24.820
I'll be happy to help you out, Onee-chan.

04:24.820 --> 04:26.200
Thanks, Anko!

04:27.140 --> 04:29.630
But I'll be expecting 
a little something in return.

04:31.420 --> 04:33.700
On second thought, maybe not.

04:33.710 --> 04:36.210
<b>The Next Day</b>

04:36.570 --> 04:37.840
On your marks!

04:38.260 --> 04:39.590
Ready...

04:42.590 --> 04:45.090
<b>Hino High</b>

04:42.590 --> 04:45.090
<b>White Team</b>

04:45.590 --> 04:49.110
<i>I somehow made everything work in time, 
but I'm absolutely beat.</i>

04:49.110 --> 04:51.310
<i>Not a single thing went according to plan.</i>

04:51.310 --> 04:54.030
<i>But I can't let this beat me!</i>

04:54.030 --> 04:55.840
<i>The main event's just begun!</i>

04:56.330 --> 04:59.610
<i>With the students, teachers, and associated 
family members as my witness...</i>

04:59.610 --> 05:04.190
<i>I will make this a magnificent sports festival 
that runs perfectly on schedule!</i>

05:04.190 --> 05:07.610
<i>That is my duty as an exemplary 
student council president!</i>

05:07.890 --> 05:09.870
<i>I'm counting on you, student council...</i>

05:10.200 --> 05:11.480
<i>and Deer Club!</i>

05:12.120 --> 05:14.870
<i>I've got my doubts about 
everyone besides Anko...</i>

05:15.680 --> 05:17.370
<i>But they're better than nothing!</i>

05:17.850 --> 05:19.990
Where the hell did Shikanoko go?!

05:19.990 --> 05:21.500
No idea.

05:21.920 --> 05:25.580
The next event will be 
the class 100-meter dash.

05:25.580 --> 05:27.380
I will now introduce our runners.

05:28.330 --> 05:29.640
So cute!

05:30.760 --> 05:32.140
<b>Deer Team</b>

05:31.120 --> 05:33.040
From the Deer Team, Nokotan.

05:31.990 --> 05:39.650
<b></b>Putting My Soul into Every Pitch

05:34.180 --> 05:35.000
Wait, what?

05:35.000 --> 05:39.650
Since when do we have a Deer Team?! 
And what's with that ridiculous getup?!

05:39.650 --> 05:42.460
Of course Nokotan would be in the Deer Team.

05:42.460 --> 05:44.150
Seriously, <i>what</i> Deer Team?!

05:46.900 --> 05:50.050
Tsubameya-san, you should be 
working! What're you doing?!

05:50.050 --> 05:54.540
Hey, Anko! What the hell's the Deer Team? 
There was nothing like that in the script!

05:54.890 --> 05:57.040
Huh? But it's written right here.

05:57.040 --> 05:57.810
See?

05:57.790 --> 05:59.540
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

05:57.790 --> 05:59.540
<b>Class 100-meter dash

Opening announcement
The next event will be the class 100-meter dash.
I will now introduce our runners.

Red Team Class 2-1 Inui-san
...
White Team Class 2-2 Kameyama-san
...
(Read the rest of the names of the runners)
Runners, please get ready.

=Begin race=</b>

05:57.790 --> 05:59.540
<b>Important!!!!!!</b>

05:57.790 --> 05:59.540
<b>Add this!</b>

05:57.790 --> 05:59.540
<b>Deer Team
Nokotan</b>

05:58.170 --> 05:59.540
She did her prep!

05:59.540 --> 06:00.880
There's a banner, too.

05:59.540 --> 06:02.290
<b>Red Team's
the Best!</b>

05:59.540 --> 06:02.290
<b>White Team's
Gonna Win</b>

05:59.540 --> 06:02.290
<b>Deer Team, Notsu!!</b>

06:00.880 --> 06:02.290
When did that go up?!

06:02.290 --> 06:04.630
Nokotan looks peak!

06:04.630 --> 06:07.800
She's too cute! I wanna get 
a pic, so look this way!

06:09.050 --> 06:11.300
Yeah, that's it! Nice!

06:16.840 --> 06:18.690
Looks like the photo session's begun.

06:18.940 --> 06:21.900
<i>Crap! At this rate, we're 
gonna run behind schedule!</i>

06:22.270 --> 06:24.940
<i>They immediately fell ten minutes behind.</i>

06:25.450 --> 06:29.070
<i>The next event is the bread-eating race 
with family members.</i>

06:29.070 --> 06:31.410
Damn you, Shikanoko.

06:31.410 --> 06:32.770
P-P-P-President!

06:32.770 --> 06:35.200
Whoa! What's the matter, Tanukikoji-san?

06:35.200 --> 06:39.460
Th-The bread for the bread-eating race...

06:39.460 --> 06:41.250
W-W-We don't have any.

06:41.660 --> 06:46.040
Huh? Why, though?! We had it all ready, 
and we double-checked the numbers!

06:47.690 --> 06:53.130
W-Well, apparently a wild bear 
came by and ate the lot!

06:53.130 --> 06:59.580
I'm sorry! It probably only ate the bread 
because it wasn't able to eat me instead!

06:59.580 --> 07:02.500
Your negativity sure goes straight 
from zero to a hundred!

07:02.500 --> 07:06.010
Anyway, wouldn't the bigger issue be 
that there's a wild bear in Hino?!

07:06.440 --> 07:08.610
I heard everything.

07:08.760 --> 07:13.240
<b>Out of Shape</b>

07:09.480 --> 07:11.470
Leave this to me!

07:11.470 --> 07:13.240
Shikanoko!

07:15.670 --> 07:17.240
Yeah, that tracks.

07:22.440 --> 07:25.820
<i>Mark my words, I'll be winning 
this family bread-eating race!</i>

07:25.820 --> 07:30.630
<i>With this show of gallantry, 
I'll earn my little sister's respect!</i>

07:31.760 --> 07:36.260
<i>I gathered all the data... 
and came up with a brilliant plan.</i>

07:37.510 --> 07:40.080
<i>I'm sorry, other family members, 
but there can only be one.</i>

07:40.440 --> 07:43.270
<i>Hm? Is that deer a family member of that girl?</i>

07:43.270 --> 07:46.860
<i>Well, no matter. 
It's time for me to seize victory.</i>

07:47.210 --> 07:49.530
<i>Step one for winning a bread-eating race...</i>

07:49.530 --> 07:52.280
<i>is to bite onto the bread just hard 
enough so it doesn't brea—</i>

07:52.600 --> 07:53.280
<i>What?!</i>

07:53.280 --> 07:54.660
<i>It's not bread!</i>

07:54.660 --> 07:56.160
Oh!

07:56.160 --> 07:59.410
Alms from the great Deer God!

08:00.350 --> 08:01.510
<i>It's eating them!</i>

08:01.510 --> 08:04.390
<i>Er, of course a deer would eat deer crackers.</i>

08:04.390 --> 08:05.440
<i>Damn it!</i>

08:10.590 --> 08:13.860
<i>M-My mouth's quickly drying out!</i>

08:13.860 --> 08:15.280
<i>What's up next?!</i>

08:17.080 --> 08:18.390
<i>Grass?!</i>

08:18.390 --> 08:20.180
<i>So bitter!</i>

08:20.180 --> 08:23.660
<i>But at this point, I won't be shocked, 
no matter what food comes up next!</i>

08:26.250 --> 08:27.150
<i>An antler?!</i>

08:27.480 --> 08:30.900
<i>Okay, I get that deer eat grass, 
so it can be considered food.</i>

08:30.900 --> 08:33.400
<i>But there's nothing edible about this antler!</i>

08:33.840 --> 08:36.410
<i>This show's established precedent 
begs to differ.</i>

08:42.870 --> 08:46.080
<i>Of course I'm not going to 
be able to outrun a deer!</i>

08:50.160 --> 08:53.880
I am protected by the great Deer God!

08:55.970 --> 09:00.600
<i>Coming in first place at the family 
bread-eating race is Inukai Mitsu-san!</i>

09:02.930 --> 09:05.290
<i>I failed to win, but I did come third.</i>

09:05.290 --> 09:11.020
<i>Maybe now my little sister will see that 
I'm more than some coffee-brewing shut-in.</i>

09:12.430 --> 09:14.400
<i>She wasn't even looking!</i>

09:14.940 --> 09:17.660
<i>The next event is the obstacle course.</i>

09:17.660 --> 09:19.530
<b>Red Team   White Team</b>

09:20.020 --> 09:24.540
<i>I haven't been in a single event yet, 
but I already feel like I've run a marathon.</i>

09:21.790 --> 09:24.540
<b>White Team</b>

09:24.540 --> 09:26.180
On your marks...

09:26.180 --> 09:27.170
Get set...

09:29.660 --> 09:33.430
<i>Ah... During a race, I don't have 
to think. I only have to run.</i>

09:33.430 --> 09:35.050
<i>What a relief...</i>

09:35.810 --> 09:37.530
<i>Oh, no. I can't fall behind.</i>

09:37.530 --> 09:41.180
<i>As a student council president who excels 
at sports, I have to get first place!</i>

09:42.030 --> 09:43.900
You're so cool, President!

09:43.900 --> 09:45.310
Koshi-san, fight on!

09:45.970 --> 09:48.940
<i>Let's see... The first obstacle is...</i>

09:51.690 --> 09:52.940
<i>Huh?</i>

09:55.210 --> 09:56.950
Wh-What is this?! A bomb?!

09:57.490 --> 09:59.800
All the obstacles involve bombs.

09:59.800 --> 10:02.200
Bombs and sports festivals do <i>not</i> mix!

10:06.470 --> 10:08.080
That voice!

10:08.330 --> 10:13.460
To raise the excitement level of this festival, 
I've leveled up the obstacles!

10:08.330 --> 10:13.460
Yakiniku Meal

10:13.460 --> 10:16.030
What the hell do you think you're doing?!

10:19.400 --> 10:25.890
<b>We are Deer Team</b>

10:19.490 --> 10:22.290
Oh, god! The school grounds!

10:22.290 --> 10:24.320
Hey! Never lower your guard on the battlefield!

10:24.320 --> 10:25.890
It's a damn schoolyard!

10:28.640 --> 10:31.550
What the hell did they teach you at school?

10:31.550 --> 10:34.650
Japanese, math, science, social studies! 
You know, general education!

10:34.650 --> 10:37.090
You're never gonna make it 
out in the real world

10:37.090 --> 10:39.110
if you can't even clear these obstacles!

10:39.110 --> 10:41.030
The real world? In what universe?!

10:41.290 --> 10:43.120
You can do it, Red Team!

10:43.120 --> 10:44.910
You can do it, White Team!

10:44.910 --> 10:48.620
You've got some nerve spouting platitudes 
when it's life or death out here!

10:48.620 --> 10:50.750
Koshitan, it's almost time.

10:50.750 --> 10:51.320
Huh?

10:54.310 --> 10:57.420
<i>It's more of a death game than a race.</i>

12:07.790 --> 12:10.510
<i>And that was a performance 
from our cheerleading squad.</i>

12:11.360 --> 12:13.370
<i>I-I'm so beat...</i>

12:15.450 --> 12:18.240
<i>But this was the final morning event.</i>

12:18.240 --> 12:20.480
<i>The club performances have ended.</i>

12:20.480 --> 12:23.630
<i>We're 15 minutes over, but if we 
cut 15 minutes off lunch break,</i>

12:23.630 --> 12:28.350
<i>we'll be back on track, and I'll fulfill 
my duty as the student council president.</i>

12:28.350 --> 12:31.640
<i>Next up, we have a performance 
by the Deer Club.</i>

12:32.640 --> 12:33.990
The Deer Club?!

12:33.990 --> 12:35.750
Let's all welcome the Deer Club.

12:35.750 --> 12:38.610
Wait! The Deer Club never signed up for this!

12:40.650 --> 12:42.500
A herd of deer...

12:42.500 --> 12:43.400
This is...

12:44.050 --> 12:45.660
<b>Compensating for My Shortcomings</b>

12:45.660 --> 12:46.930
<i>Déjà vu!</i>

12:49.460 --> 12:54.520
Hey! Who said you could sign up our club 
for another damn deer parade?!

12:54.520 --> 12:56.180
Where are we, a zoo?!

12:56.180 --> 12:58.790
Actually, even for a zoo 
this'd be out of the question!

13:05.070 --> 13:09.180
<b>Get Rich Quick</b>

13:06.870 --> 13:09.180
No, really! What the hell is this?!

13:13.140 --> 13:14.810
Wait, was there something to cry about?

13:15.140 --> 13:17.800
Tears just came flowing out...

13:17.800 --> 13:19.230
Way to go, Deer Club.

13:19.620 --> 13:22.960
I'm thinking maybe the whole reason 
I was born was to see this.

13:22.960 --> 13:25.660
Praise be! Praise be!

13:25.660 --> 13:27.540
This isn't what you think it is!

13:27.540 --> 13:29.420
You're all being tricked!

13:31.630 --> 13:33.650
Just hurry up and get the hell outta here!

13:33.650 --> 13:35.460
You're already over time!

13:36.960 --> 13:38.910
Get down here already!

13:38.460 --> 13:50.470
<b>Hino Deer
For Life</b>

13:40.050 --> 13:41.290
Whoa, there.

13:41.910 --> 13:44.720
I keep telling you we don't have time for this!

13:44.720 --> 13:48.470
<i>Will Koshitan be able to end 
the sports festival on time?</i>

13:48.470 --> 13:50.470
<i>Find out after the break!</i>

13:50.470 --> 13:53.970
<b>Nikko City, Tochigi Prefecture
Yuno Lake, Yumoto</b>

13:53.970 --> 13:57.480
<b>Nikko City, Tochigi Prefecture
Yuno Lake, Yumoto</b>

13:57.870 --> 14:01.230
<i>The first afternoon event will be tug-of-war.</i>

14:01.490 --> 14:05.240
<i>All that, and we only just 
made it to the eyecatch?</i>

14:07.860 --> 14:10.220
Ready... Start!

14:10.570 --> 14:59.800
Pull! Pull! Pull! Pull!

14:13.120 --> 14:16.500
<i>In any case, this is a proper event, 
so I need to do my best.</i>

14:16.990 --> 14:21.000
<i>Ooh? We're pulling pretty well. 
We might just have it in the bag!</i>

14:23.770 --> 14:26.180
<i>Actually, we seem to be 
pulling a bit </i>too<i> well.</i>

14:26.180 --> 14:29.240
<i>And this rope seems awkwardly smooth...</i>

14:29.240 --> 14:30.470
<i>Smooth?</i>

14:30.470 --> 14:31.970
<i>It's not even a freakin' rope!</i>

14:32.380 --> 14:33.470
<i>This texture...</i>

14:34.110 --> 14:34.970
<i>It can't be...</i>

14:34.970 --> 14:36.740
<i>It's an antler!</i>

14:38.980 --> 14:41.240
Approximately 16 seconds remain!

14:41.240 --> 14:43.540
I wonder how far each team 
will be able to stretch!

14:43.540 --> 14:45.720
That's not how tug-of-war works at all!

14:45.720 --> 14:47.490
Stop changing the damn rules!

14:47.720 --> 14:50.900
This tug-of-war—or rather, 
tug-of-antler battle is getting fired up.

14:50.900 --> 14:53.840
And you need to stop acting like 
nothing weird is happening!

14:53.840 --> 14:57.120
You're all way too accepting 
of all these crazy changes!

14:58.120 --> 15:00.220
And we're done!

15:00.220 --> 15:02.120
Uh-oh, looks like time's up.

15:02.120 --> 15:05.130
And we've got our record. It's 325 meters.

15:05.360 --> 15:06.900
Record of what?

15:06.900 --> 15:09.560
And so, the winner is Nokotan!

15:09.560 --> 15:10.130
Wha?!

15:10.130 --> 15:11.540
Yay!

15:10.130 --> 15:13.510
<b>No Reply Necessary</b>

15:11.540 --> 15:13.510
Hello? Did she even do anything?

15:13.510 --> 15:23.270
<b>Thumbs Up</b>

15:14.480 --> 15:17.590
<i>Oh? Looks like the judge 
is also giving the OK.</i>

15:17.590 --> 15:20.430
<i>Nokotan has established a new record.</i>

15:20.750 --> 15:23.270
Uh, when the hell did a judge get here?!

15:23.650 --> 15:27.780
<i>In the track-and-field game of tug-of-antler, 
a new world record has been established.</i>

15:27.780 --> 15:29.900
<i>The next event is the ball toss.</i>

15:30.350 --> 15:34.530
Okay! Please form two lines with your classes!

15:34.940 --> 15:37.790
<i>The president and I will be 
the referees for this game.</i>

15:37.790 --> 15:40.930
<i>This is the perfect opportunity 
for me to find her weakness!</i>

15:40.930 --> 15:43.670
Neko-chan is just as tiny and cute as ever!

15:43.670 --> 15:46.440
<i>Speaking of, the president sure is late.</i>

15:46.440 --> 15:50.050
Sorry... It took forever 
to finish up tug-of-antler.

15:51.470 --> 15:54.330
Eek! A-Are you all right?

15:54.330 --> 15:56.810
Your face seems to have fallen apart.

15:56.810 --> 15:58.280
I'm fine.

15:58.280 --> 16:00.930
That's exactly what someone 
who isn't fine would say.

16:01.460 --> 16:02.370
Um...

16:02.370 --> 16:03.650
Would you like some water?

16:03.650 --> 16:05.350
Maybe some stomach medicine?

16:05.350 --> 16:08.220
Actually, before that, maybe 
you should have a light snack.

16:08.220 --> 16:10.320
Do you want me to go buy you something?

16:10.540 --> 16:13.150
I'm okay... Thanks.

16:14.500 --> 16:17.690
<i>Even Neko-chan didn't have 
the heart to try to find the weakness</i>

16:17.690 --> 16:20.200
<i>of someone whose face 
had literally fallen apart.</i>

16:25.790 --> 16:27.960
Please actually aim for the baskets!

16:28.390 --> 16:30.210
Please don't stick out like that!

16:30.430 --> 16:32.840
Hey... Aim for the baskets...

16:33.140 --> 16:35.470
P-Please don't stick out like that...

16:35.470 --> 16:40.180
<i>Whew... Man, the sports festival is 
way more hectic than I thought it'd be.</i>

16:40.580 --> 16:43.850
<i>I want to hurry up and finish up work 
so Tsucchi can comfort me.</i>

16:43.850 --> 16:47.040
<i>I wonder what Tsucchi 
is doing right about now.</i>

16:47.040 --> 16:50.230
<i>I wonder if they're asleep. 
I hope they're not cold...</i>

16:51.480 --> 16:52.490
<i>Huh?</i>

16:54.470 --> 16:55.860
Tsucchi!

16:59.840 --> 17:00.980
<i>What're you doing here?!</i>

17:00.980 --> 17:02.370
<i>Er, more importantly...</i>

17:02.720 --> 17:05.120
<i>I need to protect Tsucchi!</i>

17:07.310 --> 17:09.450
<i>There's nothing here!</i>

17:10.260 --> 17:12.760
<i>Wait! Don't go out!</i>

17:12.760 --> 17:15.970
Nekoyamada-san, please get back to work...

17:15.970 --> 17:18.390
<i>And so, the game was paused.</i>

17:18.390 --> 17:22.890
<i>It was delayed 15 minutes, and Koshitan's 
stomach gained around six more holes.</i>

17:23.240 --> 17:26.460
<i>I have never been this 
exhausted in my entire life.</i>

17:26.460 --> 17:29.520
The next event is the relay race by grade.

17:31.480 --> 17:34.260
<i>But the only event left is the relay!</i>

17:34.260 --> 17:38.420
<i>My stomach's full of holes and my face 
fell apart, but it's almost over.</i>

17:38.420 --> 17:40.510
<i>This hell of a sports festival will be over!</i>

17:40.510 --> 17:42.040
President! We've got trouble!

17:42.950 --> 17:44.450
<b>Boom</b>

17:45.110 --> 17:48.990
Th-The deer have all started lounging 
around on the track, and at this rate,

17:48.990 --> 17:51.920
we won't be able to do the final relay!

17:51.920 --> 17:54.460
I just can't anymore...

17:54.920 --> 17:58.180
It's all over!

17:56.530 --> 17:57.650
<b>Sports festival failure</b>

17:57.280 --> 17:58.400
<b>Student council disbands</b>

17:58.030 --> 17:59.160
<b>Expulsion awaits</b>

17:58.780 --> 17:59.910
<b>Left with nowhere to go</b>

18:00.620 --> 18:01.720
<b>Only death awaits!</b>

18:01.720 --> 18:07.690
<b>Will</b>

18:02.680 --> 18:05.810
Uh... Seriously, your imagination 
is way out of control.

18:05.810 --> 18:07.670
B-B-B-B-But...

18:08.190 --> 18:10.160
Calm down, Tanukikoji-san.

18:10.160 --> 18:11.440
There's still a chance.

18:12.000 --> 18:13.080
<i>I know!</i>

18:13.080 --> 18:14.660
<i>That's right! It's now or never!</i>

18:14.660 --> 18:17.110
<i>Don't underestimate the guts 
of a former delinquent!</i>

18:17.500 --> 18:19.290
Now's the time for the Deer Club to act!

18:19.290 --> 18:21.280
Shikanoko... is not here.

18:21.280 --> 18:23.820
Anko... is commentating.

18:23.820 --> 18:26.080
Oh, fine! Bashame! Where are you?!

18:26.400 --> 18:27.750
Bashame's here.

18:27.750 --> 18:29.580
She's in full farming gear?!

18:30.800 --> 18:34.410
Bashame told you that she was 
getting ready to plant rice.

18:34.410 --> 18:37.590
And <i>I</i> told you to help 
with the sports festival!

18:37.590 --> 18:41.850
But Bashame already worked 
hard on maintenance.

18:41.850 --> 18:43.720
Wait, really?

18:43.720 --> 18:44.590
Of the rice paddy.

18:44.590 --> 18:46.560
Enough with the farming!

18:46.560 --> 18:51.210
Anyway, I need everyone who's free 
to help herd those deer off the track!

18:51.830 --> 18:53.360
I think you mean, "Yes, ma'am!"

18:53.360 --> 18:55.610
<b>10 minutes later...</b>

18:55.610 --> 18:57.860
P-P-Please don't eat me!

18:57.860 --> 19:00.360
Hey! Let go of Tsucchi!

19:00.580 --> 19:03.490
Just a nibble, okay?

19:05.490 --> 19:07.370
What should we do, Koshi-san?

19:07.370 --> 19:10.340
I don't think we'll be able 
to begin the relay like this.

19:10.340 --> 19:12.520
Don't worry! I'll figure something out!

19:12.520 --> 19:14.540
Really? Okay, then.

19:15.220 --> 19:17.750
<i>We're totally screwed!</i>

19:21.110 --> 19:22.800
<i>Crap. Crap. Crap.</i>

19:22.800 --> 19:24.740
<i>At this rate...</i>

19:24.820 --> 19:26.030
<b>Sports festival failure</b>

19:25.580 --> 19:26.780
<b>Student council disbands</b>

19:26.330 --> 19:27.540
<b>Failure as the student council president</b>

19:26.830 --> 19:28.040
<b>Fall from grace as an honor student</b>

19:27.580 --> 19:28.790
<b>Left with nowhere to go</b>

19:30.290 --> 19:32.650
<b>Only death awaits!</b>

19:33.360 --> 19:35.510
Yeah, no! I'm definitely overthinking this!

19:35.510 --> 19:36.650
Calm down, me!

19:36.930 --> 19:39.810
<i>Damn it! How did this happen, anyway?</i>

19:41.030 --> 19:42.410
<b>Final Return</b>

19:42.640 --> 19:44.930
It's you...

19:49.650 --> 19:52.500
Nokotan! Come here!

19:52.500 --> 19:55.230
I've got something nice waiting for you!

19:55.230 --> 19:58.070
Nokotan! Come here!

19:58.070 --> 20:00.750
I've got something nice waiting for you!

20:00.750 --> 20:03.540
Nokotan! Come here!

20:03.540 --> 20:05.770
I've got something nice...

20:05.770 --> 20:06.990
in your dreams!

20:21.420 --> 20:24.070
Hey, you damn deer!

20:33.210 --> 20:35.080
<b>Perfect Weather</b>

20:34.200 --> 20:36.790
Eat this!

20:46.000 --> 20:49.320
My secret stash of deer crackers!

20:49.320 --> 20:52.810
Shut your mouth! This whole 
event's a mess because of you!

20:52.810 --> 20:55.560
Don't go bringing a damn 
herd of deer to the school!

20:55.560 --> 20:58.190
You're always meddling with everything!

20:58.190 --> 21:00.690
I've had enough of you, you jackass!

21:06.600 --> 21:08.570
<i>N-Now I've done it!</i>

21:09.000 --> 21:12.430
<i>I lost my cool, got mad, 
and totally broke my façade.</i>

21:12.430 --> 21:16.650
<i>My life as a high school honor 
student is truly over now.</i>

21:19.710 --> 21:21.590
Koshi-san's so cool!

21:21.590 --> 21:22.590
<i>Huh?</i>

21:22.590 --> 21:25.290
Being cool comes so naturally to her.

21:25.290 --> 21:28.790
I'm totally for it. Actually, she 
seems even more relatable now.

21:28.790 --> 21:31.470
I want Koshi-san to yell at me, too.

21:31.470 --> 21:33.590
She's not afraid to put people 
in line when necessary.

21:33.590 --> 21:35.600
Truly, a wonderful student council president!

21:35.600 --> 21:37.690
That's great.

21:37.690 --> 21:41.110
It'll make it all the more worthwhile 
to drag you down.

21:41.110 --> 21:44.240
She's been showing her true self 
here and there anyway.

21:46.110 --> 21:48.110
Good for you, Koshitan.

21:48.260 --> 21:58.440
<b>Whrrrrrrrrrrrr</b>

21:48.830 --> 21:52.650
<i>Part of her was happy 
to be accepted for who she was,</i>

21:52.650 --> 21:57.710
<i>but at the same time, she wondered why 
she had worked so hard up until this point.</i>

21:59.100 --> 22:02.520
<i>By the way, the sports festival 
ran three hours late.</i>

22:02.520 --> 22:04.350
Goddamn it!
